[gd_scene load_steps=12 format=3]

; EGG-1 — THE PUFFIN LAB THROWBACK. Ported from the sibling repo mp-foundation @ 8d07fed (no
; shared git history, so a file port and not a cherry-pick):
;   Lab   = scenes/game/world/rooms/LabAuthored.tscn   -> puffinlab/LabRoom.tscn
;   Route = scenes/game/world/rooms/EscapeRouteAuthored.tscn -> puffinlab/EscapeRoute.tscn
; The two authored rooms are one continuous navigable space in the source's own coordinates and
; are instanced here unmoved, so every hard-coded position in the ported C# (the lurker at the
; door glass, the gallery crossing, the tunnel centreline) still means what it meant.
;
; SIX THINGS IN THIS FILE ARE LOAD-BEARING AND MUST NOT BE UNDONE WITHOUT READING THE REPORT:
;
;  1. THE SCALE ON Lab AND Route. The source was authored around a 0.9 m tall avatar; Sail's is
;     taller, and at 1:1 the player does not fit through the 1.05 m tiny door — which is the ONLY
;     way into the black room where ReturnTv stands. Scaling the rooms rather than widening the
;     door keeps "puffin-sized tiny doors" tiny, which is what Talon asked for by name, and makes
;     the fit a proof rather than a guess: at this ratio Sail's capsule occupies the same relative
;     volume the source's did, so anything the original could traverse, this one can.
;     PuffinLabSelfTest measures it against the live avatar's own proportions and fails if the
;     margin ever goes negative. The scale sits on the two CHILDREN, never on the root, so the
;     level that instances this scene is free to write the root's transform however it likes.
;
;  2. THE ROOT IS AT IDENTITY, and Arrival / ReturnTv are direct children of it. That is the seam
;     EGG-2 reads: Arrival's transform is where a traveller is placed, ReturnTv is the portal it
;     wires. Nothing else in this file is EGG-2's to touch.
;
;  3. THERE IS NO CanvasLayer, NO ColorRect AND NO WorldEnvironment ANYWHERE IN THIS SCENE, and
;     two of those had to be taken out rather than merely not added:
;       - LabAuthored.tscn carried a "Vignette" CanvasLayer (layer 50) holding a full-screen
;         ColorRect with a black vignette shader. A CanvasLayer draws over the WHOLE game, not
;         over the room it was authored in, so instanced into the bubble level that was a
;         permanent vignette on every screen, everywhere, from level load.
;       - It also carried a WorldEnvironment. Godot applies one per world, and the bubble level
;         has a single declared sky/ambient writer (OutdoorAtmosphere); a second one buried in an
;         easter-egg room is a fight nobody would think to look for.
;     The fade-to-black itself was never in these scenes at all — it lived in EscapeHost.cs and
;     EscapeWorld.cs, neither of which is ported. See PuffinLabRoom's class doc.
;
;  4. ReturnTv STANDS WHERE THE FADE USED TO FIRE. The source's end beat triggered on the
;     "Terminus" Area3D in the black room; the way out is now a television in that same room,
;     screen facing the tiny door so it is the first thing an arriving player sees.
;
;  5. ReturnTv AUTHORS ITS OWN Screen / ScreenGlowPool / ScreenTrigger, exactly as
;     sections/TvRoom.tscn does. TvPortal adopts all three when present and builds them only when
;     they are missing, so this keeps the geometry in the file where it can be opened and flown
;     around — and keeps the authored tv_static material on screen instead of a generated one.
;
;  6. Arrival IS AT IDENTITY ROTATION. A Sail teleport resets MoveState.Yaw to 0, i.e. -Z, so the
;     arriving player looks down the room's long axis with the cage racks and the green glow of
;     the torn wall ahead of them. Rotating this marker would describe a facing the teleport does
;     not honour.

